#ntdiff private/ntos/ke/mips/flush.c
=1 1 13
+    ARM port of KE\MIPS\FLUSH.C: a range of the instruction cache is swept
+    by virtual address on the current processor only, as on the PowerPC
+    (KE\PPC\FLUSH.C). The multiprocessing extensions broadcast cache
+    maintenance by address to every processor of the inner shareable domain,
+    where all memory is, while a target of an interprocessor request would
+    reach the address in the address space it runs, in which a user address
+    is not mapped. The whole caches are swept by set and way, which is not
+    broadcast, on every processor as on MIPS.
=1 13 45
=1 66 443
=1 511 5
+    // instruction cache, then sweep the entire instruction cache on every
+    // processor.
=1 521 3
+        KeSweepIcache(AllProcessors);
=1 710 4
+    // Write the range back from the data cache to the point of unification
+    // and invalidate it in the instruction cache, at the caller's IRQL: the
+    // operations reach every processor, and a fault on the range is taken
+    // where the caller expects it (NtFlushInstructionCache).
=1 555 6
=1 643 178
